From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configs: orangepi_zero2: keep the environment in the SPI flash

Armbian images are one ext4 partition: the default FAT environment only
prints "Unable to use mmc 0:1" on every boot, and U-Boot cannot write
Armbian's ext4 (metadata_csum), so an ext4 environment cannot be saved
either. Keep the environment in the 2 MiB SPI NOR for SD and SPI boots
alike: 64 KiB at 0xf0000, above the ~880 KiB u-boot-sunxi-with-spl.bin
that armbian-install writes at offset 0. saveenv then works from both
boot sources. A saved environment overrides the built-in defaults, also
after U-Boot updates, until `env default -a; saveenv`. Needs the sunxi
SPI flash environment fallback patch.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 CONFIG_SUN8I_EMAC=y
 CONFIG_PHY_REALTEK=y
 CONFIG_AXP305_POWER=y
+# CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT is not set
 CONFIG_SPI=y
 CONFIG_USB_EHCI_HCD=y
 CONFIG_USB_OHCI_HCD=y
